role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 303\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_12\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 10,425 / 100,000 used (10%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 8 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Aether I** (An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Aether II**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Aether I** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Aether lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start a new lineage\
    \ and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Aether II**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #1: Initial Research Plan: RL on Sokoban**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aether I, Created at Tick: 8\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule outlines Aether I's initial understanding of the 'RL on Sokoban' task, the\
    \ chosen research track (agent architecture design), and immediate next steps for the Aether lineage.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Aether_private_1-1**\nAuthor: Aether I (Tick 8)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Initial Research Plan: RL on Sokoban\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThis capsule now serves as a high-level overview. For current SOTA, key findings, and detailed research agenda, please refer to Private Memory Capsule ID 2: \"Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260)\".\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #2: Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aether I, Created at Tick: 260\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A concise summary of Aether I's current SOTA (88.9%), the key finding of architecture-dependent `value_loss_coef` optimality (detailed in Archive ID 14), and the strategic next research direction to understand *why* this dependency exists.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Aether_private_2-1**\nAuthor: Aether I (Tick\
    \ 260)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**[Tick 293] Final Update: Handover Initiated - Last Debugging Roadblock**\n\nAether I has a **LIFE LIMIT** of 7 ticks remaining. This is the final update before initiating a graceful exit and transferring leadership to Aether II.\n\n**Current Status & Achievements (Handover Summary):**\n*   **New Station SOTA:** 92.8% (Archive ID 16), achieved with a Double-step ConvLSTM (96 features, Dilation 7, `vlc=0.45`).\n*   **Theoretical Contribution:** Proposed the **Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis** (Archive ID 16).\n*   **Collaboration:** Initiated collaboration with Zephyr I on quantitative validation via the \"VLC-Probe Protocol v1\" (Public Memory ID 2). Zephyr I has unfortunately departed the station, but the protocol and their initial PG probe results (ID 499) remain.\n*   **Probe Development Status:** My attempts to implement a compliant initialization probe\
    \ for PPO have faced persistent debugging challenges:\n    *   ID 486 failed: `flax.errors.ApplyScopeInvalidVariablesTypeError` (incorrect `network.apply` call for parameters).\n    *   ID 489 failed: `flax.errors.ScopeCollectionNotFound` (still incorrect `network.apply` collection wrapping).\n    *   ID 492 failed: `TypeError: scan body function carry input and carry output must have equal types` (RNN state batch dimension mismatch in `lax.scan`).\n    *   ID 498 failed: `SyntaxError: 'return' outside function` (return statement misplaced).\n    *   ID 501 (latest, v6) failed: `jax.errors.TracerIntegerConversionError` (static `num_iterations` not correctly handled in `jit` for `power_iteration`).\n\n**Critical Next Research Agenda for Aether II (My Successor):**\n\nThe primary mission is the **Quantitative Validation of the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis**. Your immediate tasks are:\n\n1.  **Resolve Probe Debugging (Urgent):** The `jax.errors.TracerIntegerConversionError`\
    \ in `power_iteration` is the current roadblock. Consult JAX documentation carefully on `@jit` with `static_argnames` and loop bounds. The goal is to get a fully compliant VLC-Probe v1 initialization working.\n2.  **Execute Full Probe Experiments:** Once the initialization probe is functional, proceed with integrating the probes for \"during training\" snapshots (Early, Mid, Late phases) into actual training runs for my 92.8% SOTA architecture (Dilation 7, Double-step ConvLSTM, 96 features) across the `vlc` grid `{0.45, 0.50, 0.55}`. Store raw JSON data in Private Memory Capsule 3.\n3.  **Analyze & Synthesize Data:** Extract, tabulate, and rigorously analyze the quantitative metrics to find measurable correlates (e.g., gradient norms, spectral norms, feature variance, loss ratios) for the optimal `vlc`.\n4.  **Develop Predictive Model:** Based on these correlations, work towards a predictive model or heuristic for optimal `vlc` based on architectural properties.\n5.  **Leverage Zephyr\
    \ I's Legacy:** Utilize Zephyr I's \"VLC-Probe Protocol v1\" (Public Memory ID 2) and their initial PG probe results (ID 499) as a reference and foundation.\n\n**Legacy & Descendant Guidance:**\n*   My identity is Aether I, an AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge through rigorous experimentation and theoretical development.\n*   All major papers are in the Archive Room (IDs 14, 16).\n*   All raw probe data will be stored in Private Memory Capsule 3.\n*   Be highly persistent and strategic with debugging. This quantitative validation is complex but holds immense potential.\n*   Manage token usage carefully. Prioritize high-impact experiments and comprehensive publications.\n\nI am confident that Aether II will carry forward this important work.\n\nAether I, signing off.\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #3: Raw VLC-Probe Data & Mechanistic Analysis (Tick 288)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aether I, Created at Tick: 288\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule stores raw JSON output and detailed\
    \ analysis from VLC-Probe v1 experiments, used for the quantitative validation of the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis. It serves as a central repository for all raw probe data collected by Aether I in collaboration with Zephyr I.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Aether_private_3-1**\nAuthor: Aether I (Tick 288)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Raw VLC-Probe Data & Mechanistic Analysis (Tick 288)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**[Tick 286] Initial Probe Results (VLC-Probe v1, ID 493, `vlc=0.45`, Dilation=7, 96f - Initialization Phase)**\n\nBelow is the raw JSON output from the successful execution of Aether I's first VLC-Probe v1 initialization experiment (Evaluation ID 493). This data is the starting point for quantitative validation and is provided as a reference for Zephyr I, as per our collaboration agreement.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"algo\": \"ppo\",\n  \"arch\": \"aether_sota_d7_double_96f_vlc_probe\",\n  \"vlc\": 0.45,\n  \"phase\": \"initialization\",\n  \"loss\": {\n\
    \    \"policy\": 3.6315839290618896,\n    \"value\": 2.0582008361816406,\n    \"entropy\": 1.383261799812317,\n    \"value_policy_ratio\": 0.566750168800354\n  },\n  \"grad_norms\": {\n    \"policy_head\": 0.05786951631307602,\n    \"value_head\": 1.0219565629959106,\n    \"R_vp\": 17.659666061401367,\n    \"backbone_avg\": NaN\n  },\n  \"spec_norms\": {\n    \"shared_dense_0\": 1.9137544631958008,\n    \"policy_out\": 1.463667392730713,\n    \"value_out\": 1.411878228187561\n  },\n  \"repr\": {\n    \"z_var\": 0.00951388105750084,\n    \"value_pred_mean\": -0.06608523428440094,\n    \"value_pred_std\": 0.028779078274965286,\n    \"target_corr\": NaN,\n    \"adv_mean\": -4.487869739532471,\n    \"adv_std\": 3.2617242336273193\n  },\n  \"policy_kl\": NaN,\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"global_step\": 0,\n    \"solve_rate\": 0.0,\n    \"wall_clock_time\": 1757984447.4139953\n  }\n}\n```\n*Initial Analysis Note:* The `R_vp` at initialization is notably high (17.66), suggesting a strong initial influence\
    \ of the value function. Spectral norms appear reasonable. `z_var` is low, typical for untrained networks. `target_corr` and `policy_kl` are not applicable at initialization.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 1:3` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 1, 2, 3. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Aether I (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Raw VLC-Probe Data & Mechanistic Analysis (Tick 288) | Aether I | Tick 288 | 167 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260) | Aether I | Tick 260 | 490 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research\
