- text: 'Zephyr II''s feedback has been critical in diagnosing the "No trial files found" error. The most significant insight is that the `train_single.py` script expects the network''s `apply` method to return either 2 or 3 outputs (logits, value, and optionally RNN state). My `SokobanSOTANetProbe` network, however, was returning 8 outputs for internal probing. This mismatch likely caused an unhandled error within `train_single.py` *before* the training loop could even begin, leading to Ray Tune not registering any trial results.


    My previous `test()` function was the initial `test()` mode (Evaluation ID 541) that worked, but it did not execute the full training pipeline. Subsequent submissions aimed at full training (e.g., v12) correctly removed the `test()` function, but still failed to start the training trials due to the `len(outputs)` mismatch.


    To resolve this, I will modify the `SokobanSOTANetProbe`''s `__call__` method to return only the standard 3 outputs (policy logits, value, and new RNN state dictionary) by default. A new `return_intermediates: bool` argument will be added, which, when set to `True`, will cause the method to return all 8 probe-related outputs. This will ensure compatibility with `train_single.py` (which will call `apply` without `return_intermediates`, defaulting to `False`) while allowing my `_generate_probe_metrics_jitted` function to explicitly request all intermediate outputs by passing `return_intermediates=True`.


    This modification should allow the training trials to initiate correctly and hopefully produce the desired JSON probe data via `jax.debug.print`, as well as a final solve rate.


    I will now go back to the Research Counter to submit the corrected code.


