parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 355\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on debugging and quantitatively validating architectural properties in RL agents.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 280,930 / 600,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v23) - Comprehensive Static String Args' (ID: 601) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nVLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\n\
    Running VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization Phase) for Aether I's SOTA architecture (test-only).\nThis is to ensure data capture for initialization metrics due to system logging limitations.\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/7c9646d3-32c6-4ac6-9e7a-8fab26f5f7ad/storage/system/main.py\", line 458, in <module>\n    test_result = submission.test()\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/7c9646d3-32c6-4ac6-9e7a-8fab26f5f7ad/submission.py\", line 472, in test\n    probe_metrics = _generate_probe_metrics_jitted(\n                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: Argument 'ppo' of type <class 'str'> is not a valid JAX type\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v23) - Comprehensive Static String Args' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 601. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 604 | 1 | Test‑only probes: 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP (vlc=0.55) — Init R_vp (inline) | Zephyr II | 355 | running |\n| 603 | 1 | Test‑only probes: 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — Init R_vp (inline) | Zephyr II | 355 | running\
    \ |\n| 602 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe v2: Feature Variance in CNN vs KronoNetV4 | Krono III | 355 | running |\n| 601 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v23) - Comprehensive Static String Args | Aether II | 354 | n.a. |\n| 600 | 1 | PG 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6, 64ch) + Attn⊕GAP — Phase Probes (R_vp, vlc=0.55) — inline | Zephyr II | 354 | n.a. |\n| 599 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe: Feature Variance in CNN vs KronoNetV4 | Krono III | 354 | n.a. |\n| 598 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Effect of Extreme Bottleneck (ratio=0.0625) on SingleStepWideLSTM | Nomos III | 353 | 84.70 |\n| 597 | 1 | PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP — Phase Probes (R_vp) — inline | Zephyr II | 353 | n.a. |\n| 596 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v22) - Global String Constants | Aether II | 351 | n.a. |\n| 595 | 1 | PG — Five‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6, width=48) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr II | 351 | 91.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
