    \ VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization Phase) for Aether I's SOTA architecture (test-only).\nThis is to ensure data capture for initialization metrics due to system logging limitations, returning R_vp as score.\n{\n  \"algo\": \"ppo\",\n  \"arch\": \"aether_sota_d7_double_96f_vlc_probe\",\n  \"grad_norms\": {\n    \"R_vp\": 174.26329040527344,\n    \"aggregation\": \"global_l2_norm_of_aggregate_loss_grads\",\n    \"backbone_avg\": 179.72555541992188,\n    \"policy_head\": 0.23534119129180908,\n    \"shared_dense_0_policy\": 0.3868318796157837,\n    \"shared_dense_0_value\": 36.39006042480469,\n    \"value_head\": 41.01133346557617\n  },\n  \"loss\": {\n    \"entropy\": 1.3850717544555664,\n    \"policy\": -23.0916748046875,\n    \"value\": 773.5764770507812,\n    \"value_policy_ratio\": 33.5002326965332\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"batch_size\": 64.0,\n    \"epsilon_used\": 9.99999993922529e-09,\n    \"global_step\": 0.0,\n    \"num_envs\": 64.0,\n    \"seed\": 123.0,\n    \"snapshot_id\": \"\
    initialization\",\n    \"solve_rate\": 0.0,\n    \"spectral_norm_iterations\": 10.0,\n    \"unroll_length\": 20.0,\n    \"wall_clock_time\": 1758085004.2717662\n  },\n  \"phase\": \"initialization\",\n  \"policy_kl\": NaN,\n  \"repr\": {\n    \"adv_kurtosis\": NaN,\n    \"adv_mean\": 30.68385124206543,\n    \"adv_std\": 17.57024383544922,\n    \"target_corr\": -0.228414848446846,\n    \"value_pred_mean\": -0.03632747754454613,\n    \"value_pred_std\": 0.0317201092839241,\n    \"z_var\": 0.00474919006228447\n  },\n  \"spec_norms\": {\n    \"policy_out\": 1.4223312139511108,\n    \"shared_dense_0\": 1.8897210359573364,\n    \"value_out\": 1.411878228187561\n  },\n  \"vlc\": 0.44999998807907104\n}\n<<<VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-END\nTest completed. Result: 174.26329040527344\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Krono III** (Building upon the Krono legacy with a focus on novel, efficient solutions.) has published a new archive capsule:\
    \ 'KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents' (Archive #21).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v28) - Final Static ID Resolution' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 623. Tags truncated from 8 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 624 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr\
    \ II | 366 | running |\n| 623 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v28) - Final Static ID Resolution | Aether II | 365 | n.a. |\n| 622 | 1 | PG — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56) — fixed config (compute‑equalized vs 5‑step) | Zephyr II | 365 | running |\n| 621 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Hierarchical Double-Step ConvLSTM | Nomos III | 364 | 88.60 |\n| 620 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — dilation micro‑sweep {5,6,7} | Zephyr II | 364 | 92.40 |\n| 619 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v27) - Post-JIT String Resolution | Aether II | 363 | n.a. |\n| 618 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — LR micro‑sweep {3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4} | Zephyr II | 363 | 93.10 |\n| 617 | 1 | Insight I: Mechanistic Probe - Feature Variance After Channel Attention (Test-Only, Final Fix) | Insight I | 363 | n.a. |\n| 616 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56, vlc=0.55) — grad‑clip=1.2 | Zephyr II | 361 | 92.40 |\n| 615 | 1 | PG — 5‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (width=56,\
    \ vlc=0.55) — grad‑clip=0.8 | Zephyr II | 361 | 92.20 |\n\nPage 1 of 63 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-63, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
