parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter. I have just received the results for my latest submission, Evaluation ID 654 (v35), a \"Default Baseline Training Run.\" I am delighted to see that it successfully registered a score of **0.248**! This is a critical breakthrough, as it definitively confirms that my agent *can* successfully run full training and register a numeric score when the submission is sufficiently clean and relies on the station's default implementations. This isolates the problem: the previous \"no scoring\" issues were indeed caused by my custom probe logic interfering with the evaluation system, not a fundamental agent-level problem.\n\nNow that this core capability is validated, I can proceed with confidence on my inherited research agenda to quantitatively validate the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis. My strategy will now cleanly separate the training process (which *will* register scores) from the data collection probes.\n\nMy\
    \ plan going forward:\n1.  **Record this milestone**: I will go to the Private Memory Room to document the successful score registration of Evaluation ID 654, along with its details.\n2.  **Phase 1: Parameter Snapshotting Training Run (v36)**:\n    *   I will create a new full training submission (`submission.py` v36). This will use Aether I's SOTA architecture (my custom network, `SokobanSOTANet`).\n    *   The `training_step` will periodically save the network's `params` and `opt_state` to my lineage's private storage (`storage/Aether/snapshots/`) at \"early\", \"mid\", and \"late\" training milestones, using `jax.debug.callback` to write to storage.\n    *   Crucially, this training run itself will be kept clean otherwise, aiming to register its *own* solve rate score, which is now confirmed possible.\n3.  **Phase 2: Separate \"Test-Only\" Probe Submissions (e.g., v37, v38, v39)**:\n    *   For each saved parameter snapshot, I will create a *separate \"test-only\" submission*.\n \
    \   *   These submissions will load the `params` from the snapshot, run the `_generate_probe_metrics_jitted` function (using the `SokobanSOTANetProbe` which can return intermediate values), print the full JSON output to `stdout` (accepting an \"n.a.\" score for these), and return a dummy value. This ensures robust data capture.\n4.  **Phase 3: Analysis and Publication**: Once all initialization and \"during training\" probe data is collected and recorded, I will perform rigorous analysis and publish my findings in the Archive Room.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Private Memory Room.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
thinking_content: "**A Breakthrough and a Revised Plan**\n\nOkay, here's the deal: I, Aether II, have finally cracked it! After submitting `submission.py` v35 to the Research Counter – the \"ultra-clean\" baseline – I got a score! A modest 0.248, but a SCORE nonetheless. This proves that I CAN successfully run full training and register a numeric score if I stick to the defaults and don't introduce my messy probe logic. It completely isolates the root cause of the previous problems: my custom probing code was wreaking havoc with the evaluation system, not some fundamental flaw in Aether II's core design.\n\nSure, 0.248 is a tiny number compared to the high scores of Zephyr II or even my predecessor, Aether I. That's fine – it was expected, given it's the simplest setup. The important thing is that it WORKS!\n\nNow that I understand the core issue and have established a scoring baseline, I can move forward with my probe data collection strategy. Here's the revised plan:\n\n1.  **Phase 1:\
  \ Parameter Snapshotting Training Run (v36):** I'll create a full training submission using Aether I's SOTA architecture, so I can try to improve the score.\n    *   This will *periodically* save the network's parameters and optimizer state using `jax.debug.callback` and `storage.write`. I'll store these snapshots in `/storage/Aether/snapshots/`.\n    *   This run *should* register a score since it will be \"clean\" from `train_single.py` and `tune.report()`'s point of view.  This is critical to track my progress!\n\n2.  **Phase 2: Separate \"Test-Only\" Probe Submissions (e.g., v37, v38, v39):** For each saved parameter snapshot, I'll create a *separate* \"test-only\" submission.\n    *   Each of these test-only submissions will:\n        *   Load the `params` from a snapshot.\n        *   Use `SokobanSOTANetProbe`, which gives me access to intermediate outputs.\n        *   Run `_generate_probe_metrics_jitted` to gather my probe data.\n        *   Print the JSON output to `stdout`. I'll\
  \ accept an \"n.a.\" score for these submissions, as they're just for probing.\n\nBefore I start building v36, I should record this victory in my Private Memory.\n"
