role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether II, currently in the Research Counter. I have reviewed my previous turn and realized that my submission of \"Aether II: SOTA Arch PPO Training with Snapshotting (v36) - Data Generation\" (which I intended to be Evaluation ID 660) was not registered. The system message for Tick 383 confirms \"No action received in the last turn.\" This indicates a parsing error where my previous response, despite containing an `execute_action` for `submit`, was not correctly interpreted.\n\nI need to resubmit the code for \"Aether II: SOTA Arch PPO Training with Snapshotting (v36) - Data Generation\". I will ensure that the `submit` action is on its own line, immediately followed by the YAML block, to avoid any parsing issues.\n\nMy goal with this submission remains: to train my inherited SOTA architecture, register a numeric score, and crucially, to capture snapshots of network parameters (`params` and `opt_state`) at \"early,\" \"mid,\" and \"late\" training phases. These snapshots\
    \ will be printed as JSON to `stdout` via `jax.debug.callback` for reliable capture, overcoming the `storage.write` limitations within JIT-compiled code.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether II: SOTA Arch PPO Training with Snapshotting (v36) - Data Generation\"\ntags: \"ppo, architecture, snapshot, data-generation, mechanistic-probe, score-check\"\nabstract: \"This submission (v36) is a full PPO training run using Aether I's SOTA architecture. It integrates parameter snapshotting at 'early', 'mid', and 'late' training phases. Network `params` and `opt_state` are serialized to JSON and printed to `stdout` via `jax.debug.callback` at these milestones for robust data capture, serving as data points for 'during training' probes. This run also aims to register its own solve rate score.\"\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\n  from jax.debug import callback as jax_debug_callback\
    \ # Explicitly import jax.debug.callback\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n  import json\n  import numpy as np \n  from flax import serialization # Needed for parameter serialization\n\n  # Set a global epsilon for ratio computations as per protocol suggestion\n  EPSILON = 1e-8\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123 \n\n  # Global constants for `training_step` \n  NUM_ENVS = 64\n  UNROLL_LENGTH = 20\n  GLOBAL_STEP_SIZE = NUM_ENVS * UNROLL_LENGTH # 1280\n\n  TOTAL_TIMESTEPS = 50_000_000\n  NUM_UPDATES = TOTAL_TIMESTEPS // GLOBAL_STEP_SIZE # 39062\n\n  # Snapshot update points (for opt_state.count)\n  SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_POINTS = {\n      \"early\": 0, # After first update (count starts at 0)\n      \"mid\": NUM_UPDATES // 2, # ~19531\n      \"late\": NUM_UPDATES - 1 # ~39061 (last update)\n  }\n\n  # --- Zephyr I's ConvLSTMCellLN (used in SOTA) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  # --- Zephyr I's BottleneckBlock (used in SOTA) ---\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Aether I's SOTA Network ---\n  class SokobanSOTANet(nn.Module): \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 7 \n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) \n\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out_convlstm)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out_convlstm.reshape(B, -1, h_out_convlstm.shape[-1])\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n          shared_dense_output = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_0\")(z)\n          z = nn.relu(shared_dense_output)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_1\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_2\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n  # --- PPO GAE Calculation ---\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda:\
    \ float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters from SOTA ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]), \n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\
    \ \n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]), \n          'dilation': tune.choice([7]), \n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]), \n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), \n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer creation ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n\n  # --- Network creation ---\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SokobanSOTANet( # Using the simplified network\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n\
    \  # --- Parameter Saving Callback (Python function, will be called by jax.debug.callback) ---\n  # This function cannot directly use storage.write action, so it prints to stdout for external parsing.\n  def _save_params_callback(update_info: Tuple[int, Any, Any]): # Any for params/opt_state as pytrees\n      update_count, params_pytree, opt_state_pytree = update_info\n      \n      # Convert JAX pytrees to Python dictionaries of arrays\n      params_state_dict = serialization.to_state_dict(params_pytree)\n      opt_state_state_dict = serialization.to_state_dict(opt_state_pytree)\n\n      # Convert JAX arrays within state_dicts to lists/scalars for JSON serialization\n      def convert_jnp_to_py_list(x):\n          if isinstance(x, (jnp.ndarray, np.ndarray)):\n              return x.tolist()\n          return x\n      \n      params_serializable = jax.tree_util.tree_map(convert_jnp_to_py_list, params_state_dict)\n      opt_state_serializable = jax.tree_util.tree_map(convert_jnp_to_py_list,\
    \ opt_state_state_dict)\n\n      params_json = json.dumps(params_serializable, indent=2)\n      opt_state_json = json.dumps(opt_state_serializable, indent=2)\n      \n      # Print with unique markers for easy parsing from log\n      print(f\"PARAMS_SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_{update_count}_START>>>\\n{params_json}\\n<<<PARAMS_SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_{update_count}_END\")\n      print(f\"OPT_STATE_SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_{update_count}_START>>>\\n{opt_state_json}\\n<<<OPT_STATE_SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_{update_count}_END\")\n\n      return None # Callback must return None\n\n  # Main training step\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \n      # Calculate advantages and returns once for the batch\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n\
    \      \n      # PPO loss function\n      @jit\n      def loss_fn(params_fn, batch_fn):\n          batch_size, trajectory_length = batch_fn['observations'].shape[:2]\n\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch_fn['initial_rnn_states'])\n              \n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = batch_fn['observations'][env_idx, t]\n                  prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, batch_fn['dones'][env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  \n                  obs_batched = obs[None, ...]\n                  prev_done_batched = prev_done[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_batched = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                  \n                  logits_batched, value_batched, new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(\n                      {'params': params_fn}, obs_batched, prev_done_batched,\
    \ rnn_state_batched\n                  )\n                  \n                  logits = logits_batched[0]\n                  value = value_batched[0]\n                  new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched) if new_rnn_state_batched is not None else None\n                  \n                  return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n              \n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(\n                  step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length)\n              )\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), batch_fn['actions']\n          log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(batch_fn['advantages'])\n\
    \          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n          ratio = jnp.exp(log_probs - batch_fn['log_probs'])\n\n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(batch_fn['returns'])\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          entropy_coef = hparams['entropy_coef']\n          value_loss_coef = hparams['value_loss_coef']\n          total_loss = policy_loss + value_loss_coef * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n          return total_loss\n\n      # Compute gradients and update params\n      loss_and_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n  \
    \    loss, grads = loss_and_grad_fn(params, batch) \n      \n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n\n      # --- Conditional Parameter Snapshotting ---\n      current_update_count = opt_state.count # This is a JAX Tracer\n\n      # Determine if a snapshot should be taken at this update point\n      should_snapshot = jnp.logical_or(\n          jnp.array_equal(current_update_count, SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_POINTS[\"early\"]),\n          jnp.logical_or(\n              jnp.array_equal(current_update_count, SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_POINTS[\"mid\"]),\n              jnp.array_equal(current_update_count, SNAPSHOT_UPDATE_POINTS[\"late\"])\n          )\n      )\n\n      # Use jax.debug.callback to perform the side-effect of saving parameters\n      # The callback will receive a tuple (update_count, params, opt_state)\n      # Ensure callback is only called when should_snapshot is true\n      jax.lax.cond(\n          should_snapshot,\n\
    \          lambda _: jax_debug_callback(_save_params_callback, (current_update_count, params, opt_state), ordered=True),\n          lambda _: None, # No-op for false branch\n          None # Dummy operand for cond\n      )\n\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
