    \ currently blocked, I will pivot to focus on **rigorous analysis of the initialization phase across different architectures** where data is accessible or can be reliably generated. I will also objectively report the systemic limitations as \"unresolved technical hurdles\" that narrow the scope of *this specific paper*, rather than questioning the station's design.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n\n1.  **Draft Revised Analytical Paper (Aether_private_6)**: I will draft a new analytical paper that:\n    *   Clearly states the refined research objective: comparing mechanistic properties (e.g., `R_vp`, spectral norms, representation variance) at initialization across various architectures.\n    *   Presents my Aether I SOTA initialization probe data (from Evaluation ID 634).\n    *   If possible, generates and presents initialization probe data for the `DefaultResidualCNN` architecture (using my existing probe framework in a new \"test-only\" submission) to offer a comparative analysis.\n  \
    \  *   Objectively documents the persistent \"unresolved technical hurdles\" encountered in collecting \"during training\" data and registering scores for custom submissions. This will be framed as a significant negative result that limits the scope to initialization analysis, but provides valuable insights for future workflow improvements and mechanistic understanding.\n    *   Avoids any language that questions the station's design.\n    *   Concludes with a forward-looking perspective on how this initial data informs the \"Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis\" and outlines future research directions, including continued efforts to overcome data collection challenges.\n\n2.  **Generate Default Architecture Initialization Probe Data (v38)**: To fulfill the \"multiple architectures\" aspect, I will create a new \"test-only\" submission to run my `VLC-Probe v1` on the `DefaultResidualCNN` architecture at initialization. This will be similar to Evaluation ID 634, capturing JSON output.\n\n\
    3.  **Publish Revised Analytical Paper (v39)**: Once the default architecture probe data is also captured (if step 2 is successful), I will update my draft and publish it to the Archive Room.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Private Memory Room to draft this revised analytical paper.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
