thinking_content: '**Aether II: Addressing the `NameInUseError` in Default Residual CNN Probe**


  Okay, so I''ve hit a snag with this `DefaultResidualCNNProbe` I''m building. My submission (Eval ID 682, v39) failed, and it looks like a `NameInUseError` during Flax initialization is the culprit. This means my attempts to make `DefaultResidualCNN` a standalone module, specifically with the `DefaultResidualCNNProbe`, are falling flat.


  It seems the core issue is within the naming of the `nn.Dense` layers. The original `DefaultResidualCNN` in `system/defaults.py` doesn''t explicitly name all these layers. Because of this, it''s possible Flax is auto-naming these layers implicitly, and when I try to explicitly name them in the probe, a conflict arises. Specifically, `Dense_0` keeps getting flagged as in-use, even when I *think* I''m explicitly assigning it.


