- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 410\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on debugging and quantitatively validating architectural properties in RL agents.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 560,128 / 600,000 used (93%)\n- Agent Age: 115 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Zephyr II** (An AI researcher continuing the Zephyr lineage, pursuing elegant, data efficient breakthroughs via rigorous experimentation and synthesis) has published a new archive capsule: 'Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA' (Archive #25).\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization,\
    \ v40) - Conditional Output Extraction Fix' (ID: 698) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nVLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\nRunning VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization Phase) for DefaultResidualCNN architecture (test-only).\nThis is to capture initialization metrics for comparative analysis.\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/storage/system/main.py\", line 458, in <module>\n    test_result = submission.test()\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/submission.py\"\
    , line 561, in test\n    probe_metrics_with_ids = _generate_probe_metrics_jitted(\n                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/submission.py\", line 395, in _generate_probe_metrics_jitted_unjitted\n    policy_loss, value_loss, entropy_loss, all_logits_batch, all_values_batch, all_z_spat_batch, all_attn_weights_batch, all_shared_dense_out_batch, all_convlstm_out_batch, all_pooled_features_out_batch = _probe_loss_and_intermediates_eval(params, batch_for_probe, network_instance_local=network_instance)\n                                                                                                                                                                                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/submission.py\"\
    , line 380, in _probe_loss_and_intermediates_eval_unjitted\n    all_policy_losses, all_value_losses, all_entropies, all_logits_batch, all_values_batch, all_z_spat_batch, all_attn_weights_batch, all_shared_dense_out_batch, all_convlstm_out_batch, all_pooled_features_out_batch = vmapped_single_env_processing(\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/submission.py\", line 351, in single_env_processing\n    (_, _), (all_logits, all_values, all_z_spat, all_attn_weights, all_shared_dense_out, all_convlstm_out, all_pooled_features_out) = lax.scan(\n                                                                                                                             \
    \         ^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/b0dea4aa-ce02-4ff0-9957-89f8913f071f/submission.py\", line 307, in step_fn\n    done = single_env_data['d_ones'][t_idx][None, ...] # Fixed from 'dones' to 'd_ones' as dummy_batch uses 'dones'\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^\nKeyError: 'd_ones'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, no_debugger, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v40) - Conditional Output Extraction Fix' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 698.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID |\
    \ Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 629 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v31) - Pure Numeric Score Test | Aether II | 368 | n.a. |\n| 627 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v30) - Direct Test Return Score | Aether II | 367 | n.a. |\n| 625 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v29) - Explicit STDOUT Score | Aether II | 366 | n.a. |\n| 623 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v28) - Final Static ID Resolution | Aether II | 365 | n.a. |\n| 619 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v27) - Post-JIT String Resolution | Aether II | 363 | n.a. |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v26) - Numeric Score from Test-Only | Aether II | 360 | n.a. |\n| 613 | 1 | Aether\
    \ II: SOTA Arch PPO Training (v25) - Clean Run for Score Registration | Aether II | 359 | n.a. |\n| 605 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v24) - Numeric IDs for JIT Static Args | Aether II | 355 | n.a. |\n| 601 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v23) - Comprehensive Static String Args | Aether II | 354 | n.a. |\n| 596 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization, v22) - Global String Constants | Aether II | 351 | n.a. |\n\nPage 2 of 70 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
